;; Type System Test: storing a qubit in an untyped container is a violation
;; EXPECT-MODE: default
;; EXPECT-COMPILE: fail
;; EXPECT-STDERR: escapes into an untyped container
;; EXPECT-STDERR: Refusing to generate code for a program that violates linear

;; #471 measured `(vector q)` then two `vector-ref` as accepted, silently, with
;; no diagnostic of any kind (BI-3). The container's type carries no linearity,
;; so once the qubit is inside it every read is an unchecked use and a
;; name-keyed analysis cannot follow it.
;;
;; A bare reference handed to a container constructor or mutator is therefore
;; recorded as an ESCAPE and reported. That verdict is drawn only AFTER the use
;; count has had its say, so `(cons q q)` -- see qubit_no_cloning_default_test
;; -- still reads as the clone it is rather than as an escape.
;;
;; Note this is about a BARE reference. `(cons (h q) '())` stores the fresh
;; qubit a gate returned, not the tracked binding, and that value is not tracked
;; by name at all -- see qubit_linear_container_of_results_ok_test.esk.
(define (h (q : Qubit)) : Qubit q)
(define (z (q : Qubit)) : Qubit q)

(define (stash (q : Qubit))
  (let ((v (vector q)))
    (cons (h (vector-ref v 0)) (z (vector-ref v 0)))))
